From 37bf92ae5ad556ed82a6c1f5518434815ea30d9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 13:54:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] =?UTF-8?q?arch/dadao:=20G1=20core=20ISA=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20halt/addi/add/jump=20run=203=20smokes=20on=20gem5?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implement the DG-002a G1 core instructions with a real register-operand
pipeline and run the three E2E smokes to matching QEMU exit codes:
  smoke_arith (addi rd1,rd0,42; halt rd1)                 -> exit 42
  smoke_add   (addi;addi; add rd0,rd3,rd1,rd2; halt rd3)  -> exit 42
  smoke_jump  (jump 1; halt rd1; addi rd1,rd0,0; halt rd1)-> exit 0

Semantics derived from contracts/isa/spec.md + tools/opcodes.yaml:
  halt (op 0x00): exitSimLoop with rd[ha] value (spec §3.1)
  addi (op 0x19, rrii): rdha = rdhb + sext12(imm)          (spec §3.6)
  add  (op 0x1A, rrrr): rdha:rdhb = rdhc + rdhd, 128-bit   (spec §3.5)
  jump (op 0x64, iiii): PC = rb0 + (sext24(imm)<<2),
                        rb0 = current_PC + 4               (spec §5.3/§1.3)
rd0 reads as 0 / discards writes (skip operand when reg==0).

Each StaticInst declares src/dest RegId member arrays, calls setRegIdxArrays
(gem5 pointer-to-member idiom, per riscv insts), and uses ExecContext
getRegOperand/setRegOperand. Decoder reads instructions big-endian (betoh),
matching the DADAO ISA byte order (spec §2.1).

Restores the DG-001a SE bridge that had regressed: se_workload.{cc,hh}
(SEWorkload + Process::Loader), Process on ProcessParams, DADAOSeWorkload as an
SEWorkload SimObject. gen_min_elf.py now emits e_machine 0xda0 at a page-aligned
in-range load address; dadao_se.py uses a timing CPU + SEWorkload.init_compatible
and exits with the halt code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
